<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="F_InitTestBP" Id="{872b1e54-dad7-464f-b50c-ec80c2c884b3}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    F_InitTestBP - build a beam-parameter set whose fields are in the "OK"
    state, for use as test data in the PMPS test suites.

    PURPOSE
        Give a test one place to obtain an ST_BeamParams that describes "the
        beam is fine" - every status-bearing field at its non-faulting value -
        instead of each test spelling out all the members itself. Tests then
        override only the one or two members the assertion under test depends
        on, which keeps them readable and keeps a change to ST_BeamParams from
        having to be replayed in every test.

    USAGE
        Call it where a test needs a starting BP set and assign the result:
            stBp : ST_BeamParams;
            stBp := F_InitTestBP(stBp);
        The function is stateless and reads no global state, so it may be
        called from any TcUnit test method without side effects.
        NOTE: there are no callers today. The POU is part of the PMPS.plcproj
        compile list but nothing in the library references it; the
        beam-parameter tests in TestComponents/FB_SafeBPCompare_Test build
        their data with F_SetBeamParams instead, and that is the helper still
        in use.

    OBJECTIVES
        - One definition of "OK" test data, so tests cannot drift apart on what
          a healthy BP set looks like.
        - Test code that shows only what the test is about.
        - Absorb future additions to ST_BeamParams in a single place.

    HISTORY
        2020-11-18 / Alex Wallace
            Function added in "Tests for the margin logic" (commit 16e0988)
            together with the first TcUnit beam-parameter tests. It was created
            with an empty body and has never been called.
        2026-09-16 / Yann Stephen Mandza
            The XAE ProductVersion attribute was dropped from the TcPlcObject
            element (commit f77073f). No code change.
        2026-11-27 / Scirix Agent
            Added this header and the inline comment on BP; declaration and body
            unchanged (audit finding #256, convention conv_321640e095c0).

    NOTE
        The implementation is empty, so the function does not currently do what
        the purpose above describes: it never reads BP and never assigns its
        return value, so a caller gets the ST_BeamParams field defaults declared
        in the DUT - nTran 0, nRate 0, neVRange 0, neV 0, nBCRange 0,
        nBeamClass 0, nMachineMode 3, astAttenuators all 0, astApertures
        1000 mm x 1000 mm (fully open), aVetoDevices all FALSE, xValid FALSE,
        nCohortInt 0 - i.e. a beam-off set, not an "all status bits OK" one.
        Do not treat the result as a ready-to-use BP until the body is filled
        in.
*)
FUNCTION F_InitTestBP : ST_BeamParams
VAR_INPUT
    BP : ST_BeamParams; // BP set handed in by the caller, a complete ST_BeamParams:
                        // nTran = requested pre-optic transmission, 0..1 of full
                        //   transmission (1.0 = 100 %, per HOPR 1 / LOPR 0 and
                        //   PMPS_GVL.TRANS_SCALING_FACTOR); nRate = pulse rate in Hz;
                        // neVRange = photon-energy range bit mask; nBCRange = beam-class
                        //   range bit mask; astAttenuators = per-attenuator transmission
                        //   in %; astApertures = Width/Height in mm. Not read by the
                        //   empty body - see NOTE in the header above.
END_VAR
VAR
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>